# Source-of-Truth, OSS/Cloud, and Vertical Boundaries

## Source-of-truth (conceptual)

```text
PostgreSQL → TX4 domain persistence
TX4 core → business / domain authority
External payment provider → provider-side payment authority
Reconciliation → TX4 orchestration of differences (explicit records)
```

- Do not create competing authoritative balances or duplicated SoT without an explicit ADR
- Provider-specific concepts stay behind adapters; do not leak into public TX4 API
- If a SoT boundary is unclear: **STOP and report** (ADR-004 when resolving)

## OSS vs Managed Cloud

```text
TX4 OSS → core transaction infrastructure (self-hostable)
TX4 Managed Cloud → proprietary hosted control plane / operations
```

Do not:

- move proprietary cloud functionality into OSS without authorization
- cripple OSS for artificial commercial differentiation
- leak managed-cloud assumptions into the core domain
- introduce SaaS-only dependencies into OSS core without an explicit decision

Exact boundary remains OPEN until ADR-008 is frozen — do not silently decide it.

## Vertical-agnostic core

Dogfood apps (canteen, booking, marketplace) **consume** TX4; they do not define it.

Forbidden in generic core:

```text
if vertical == "canteen" / "booking" / "marketplace"
```

- Reusable need → extract a generic infrastructure primitive
- Vertical-specific need → keep outside core
